@startuml AopProxyFlow
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20
skinparam BoxPadding 14
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #fffff0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #aaaaaa

actor Caller

box "Spring container" #e8f4ff
  participant "**Proxy**\n(JDK dynamic proxy\nor CGLIB subclass)" as proxy #c8dfff
  participant "**@Before**\n**@Around** (pre)" as before #fffbcc
  participant "**RealBean**\n.someMethod()" as bean #d4f7d4
  participant "**@After**\n**@AfterReturning**\n**@AfterThrowing**\n**@Around** (post)" as after #ffd6d6
end box

Caller -> proxy : someMethod(args)
note right of proxy
  Container hands out the Proxy,
  never the real bean directly.
  Weaving = this swap happens at
  startup (BeanPostProcessor).
end note

proxy -> before : fire pre-advice
activate before
before --> proxy : (continue)
deactivate before

proxy -> bean : proceed() / forward call
activate bean
bean --> proxy : return value  OR  exception
deactivate bean

alt normal return
  proxy -> after : fire @AfterReturning + @After
else exception thrown
  proxy -> after : fire @AfterThrowing + @After
end

after --> proxy
proxy --> Caller : return value / rethrow exception

note over before, after
  **@Around** owns BOTH sides — it calls proceed() itself.
  It is the only advice that can:
    • modify method arguments before the call
    • modify / replace the return value
    • swallow an exception or throw a different one
    • skip the real method entirely (don't call proceed())

  All other advice types cannot stop or alter the call —
  they can only throw an exception to abort.
end note

note over proxy
  **Self-invocation pitfall**
  If RealBean calls this.otherMethod() internally,
  that call goes directly to the real object, NOT through
  the proxy → no advice fires for that internal call.
end note
@enduml
